   "title": "How to use · v1.0.0",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · v1.0.0\n\n**What it does:** Kandinsky 5 Video Lite (2B) text to video with the 16-step distilled model: 768x512, 121 frames = 5 s at 24 fps, no sound. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs** (green group): write the **Prompt** (what happens, the light, how the camera moves). Set **Width** / **Height** (768x512 default), **Frames** (121 = 5 s), **Steps** (16), **CFG** (1) and **Seed**.\n2. **Models**: the three loaders must show the files from the Downloads note.\n3. **Prompt**: the negative prompt box does nothing at CFG 1. It only counts with the sft model at CFG 5.\n4. **Sampling**: euler_ancestral / beta, shift 5, from the official template.\n5. Press **Run**. The clip is saved by the **Result** node to `output/video/`.\n\n**What to expect:** the 5 s clip took 3 min 35 s on the test card (16 steps, model load included). VRAM sat at 12.4 GB while sampling and peaked at 17.3 GB for about 20 s while decoding the video. On a smaller card ComfyUI should decode in tiles instead; that was not tested.\n\n**Best quality: the sft model.** In group 2 pick `kandinsky5lite_t2v_sft_5s.safetensors`, set **Steps** to 50 and **CFG** to 5 in group 1. Measured once: 19 min 55 s for the same clip, the frames looked more like a photo. That run used the same graph with CFG 5 typed on the sampler.\n\n**Why 16 steps and CFG 1:** the distilled model was trained to finish in 16 steps without guidance. Any CFG above 1 runs the model twice per step, so it doubles the time. Other values were not tested with this model.\n\n**Tips**\n- This is the 5 s model: the authors give 5 s (121 frames) as its limit.\n- Width and Height must be multiples of 16. Only 768x512 was tested.\n- Fewer frames = less work per step (49 = 2 s). Not tested.\n\n**Tested on:** RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB · 64 GB RAM · ComfyUI 0.45.3 started with --reserve-vram 12 (ComfyUI keeps its models within about 12 GB). **Not verified on a 12 GB card.**\n"
   ]
  },
